#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0389 expect=violation domain=TP
#note "Authority: SEND Conformance Rules v5.0 SEND389 (SENDIG-DART 1.1/1.2), Rule 'TP.RSTGCD = TT.RSTGCD'; Plain Text: 'The values of RSTGCD used in the Trial Repro Paths dataset must match values for the same Repro Stage in the Trial Repro Stages dataset.' Row 3: path F0F's third stage uses RSTGCD=LACT, which TT does not define (TT has PREMAT, MAT, GEST) -> FIRES. Rows 1, 2, 4 and 5 use TT stage codes -> silent. ALSO THE S3 FOREIGN-DISCRIMINATION PIN (SKELETON-distinct-function hazard 3): LACT exists only in the primary TP, so a port that read RSTGCD from TP instead of TT would find row 3's own value in its own set and fall silent."
#library standard=sendig-dart version=1-2
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=3 RPATHCD=F0F RSTGCD=LACT
dataset TP class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Paths"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col RPATHCD  type=Char label="Reproductive Path Code"
col RPATH    type=Char label="Reproductive Path"
col TPSTGORD type=Num  label="Planned Order of Repro Stage"
col RSTGCD   type=Char label="Repro Stage Code"
---
S1 | TP | F0F | F0 Female | 1 | PREMAT
S1 | TP | F0F | F0 Female | 2 | MAT
S1 | TP | F0F | F0 Female | 3 | LACT
S1 | TP | F0M | F0 Male   | 1 | PREMAT
S1 | TP | F0M | F0 Male   | 2 | MAT
---

dataset TT class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Repro Stages"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col RSTGCD  type=Char label="Repro Stage Code"
col RSTAGE  type=Char label="Description of Repro Stage"
col TTDUR   type=Char label="Planned Duration of Repro Stage"
---
S1 | TT | PREMAT | Premating | P14D
S1 | TT | MAT    | Mating    | P14D
S1 | TT | GEST   | Gestation |
---
